hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21415","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: a man he named narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Abdullah al-Ashari narrated to us: Isa ibn Jariyah narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdullah from Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did a deed tonight. He said: What is it. He said: Women with me in the house said to me: You recite and we do not recite, so lead us in prayer, so I prayed eight and the witr. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent. He said: So we deemed his silence approval of what was done."
"21416","Abdullah narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Shabab月的h from Shubah from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized him."
